# Requisições de exemplo — extensão "REST Client" do VS Code (humao.rest-client).
# Clique em "Send Request" acima de cada bloco. O cookie de sessão é guardado
# e reenviado automaticamente entre as requisições.
#
# Para gerar o código TOTP sem o celular (use a manualKey do passo 2a):
#   node -e "require('otplib').generate({ secret: 'MANUAL_KEY' }).then(console.log)"

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# @baseUrl = https://<app>.onrender.com

### Health check (público)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

#######################################################################
# FLUXO DO TÉCNICO
#######################################################################

### 1. Login — etapa 1 (senha)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@inventory.local", "password": "Tech@123" }

### 2a. Primeiro acesso — gera o QR Code e a chave manual
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/2fa/setup

### 2a. Primeiro acesso — confirma o primeiro código do app e ativa o 2FA
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/2fa/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "123456" }

### 2b. Acessos seguintes — código atual do app
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/2fa/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "123456" }

### Quem está logado e até quando o 2FA vale
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Estoque (com valor em R$ — AwesomeAPI)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/equipment

### Estoque filtrado
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/equipment?status=available&type=notebook

### Detalhe de um equipamento
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/equipment/1

### Histórico de empréstimos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/loans

### Empréstimos ativos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/loans?status=active

### Novo empréstimo (prazo em dias úteis, pulando feriados — BrasilAPI)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "equipment_id": 4,
  "borrower_name": "João Lima",
  "destination_department": "Financeiro",
  "business_days": 10,
  "notes": "Auditoria"
}

### Registrar devolução
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/loans/4/return

### Técnico tentando rota de admin → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### Depois do logout → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

#######################################################################
# FLUXO DO ADMIN (faça login + 2FA com admin@inventory.local antes)
#######################################################################

### Login do admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@inventory.local", "password": "Admin@123" }

### Listar contas
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### Detalhar conta
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2

### Criar conta (nasce sem 2FA)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Diego Alves", "email": "diego@inventory.local", "password": "Tech@123", "role": "technician" }

### Editar conta (todos os campos são opcionais)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/5
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Diego A. Alves", "active": false }

### Resetar o 2FA (técnico perdeu o celular)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/reset-2fa

### Excluir conta (usuários com empréstimos não podem ser excluídos → 409)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/5

### Admin tentando ver o estoque → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/equipment

#######################################################################
# ERROS
#######################################################################

### 400 — corpo inválido
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nao-e-email", "password": "" }

### 401 — senha errada
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@inventory.local", "password": "errada" }

### 401 — código com formato certo mas inválido (5 seguidos → 423)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/2fa/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "000000" }
